{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836776",
      "title": "Preparing the App For Data Fetching",
      "sourceHash": "23dc1c08887fbaa56c4d747b3ead6c5c448f4d364a98b3d900477b67a1432b47",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.866,
          "end": 2.866,
          "en": "- [Maximilian] So let's establish a connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.866,
          "end": 6.166,
          "en": "between the React app and this dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.333,
          "end": 9.133,
          "en": "Now, for this you must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.133,
          "end": 12.033,
          "en": "that the backend server is also up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.033,
          "end": 15.666,
          "en": "and therefore when following along locally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.666,
          "end": 19.533,
          "en": "it's actually not just enough to run npm run dev.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.533,
          "end": 22.733,
          "en": "Instead, in a separate terminal window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.733,
          "end": 26.7,
          "en": "so that you keep the npm run dev process up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.7,
          "end": 29.966,
          "en": "you should cd the into the backend folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.966,
          "end": 32.866,
          "en": "and then in there, run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.866,
          "end": 35.866,
          "en": "to install the dependencies of this backend project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.2,
          "end": 37.666,
          "en": "Because it's a separate project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.833,
          "end": 40.033,
          "en": "it's a separate server that will start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.566,
          "end": 45.033,
          "en": "After running npm install in that backend folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.333,
          "end": 47.666,
          "en": "you must start the backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.666,
          "end": 51.733,
          "en": "because we're dealing with two separate servers now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.333,
          "end": 55.166,
          "en": "the frontend Vite development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.533,
          "end": 58.3,
          "en": "which serves the frontend, the React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.666,
          "end": 60.666,
          "en": "and the separate backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.833,
          "end": 62.566,
          "en": "which exposes this backend API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.066,
          "end": 65.566,
          "en": "And you start this backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.566,
          "end": 69.93299999999999,
          "en": "by running node app.js in that backend folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.066,
          "end": 72.866,
          "en": "so in that terminal where you navigated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.866,
          "end": 74.233,
          "en": "into the backend folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.466,
          "end": 80.46600000000001,
          "en": "Now for this to work, you actually need to install Node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.833,
          "end": 83.833,
          "en": "Again, on CodeSandbox that's not necessary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.833,
          "end": 85.8,
          "en": "There it will automatically run,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.8,
          "end": 89.26599999999999,
          "en": "but locally if you wanna follow along there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.26599999999999,
          "end": 93.233,
          "en": "you have to install Node.js on your system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.233,
          "end": 97.066,
          "en": "It is available for Mac OS, Windows, and Linux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.066,
          "end": 101.26599999999999,
          "en": "And once you did that, you can and should run node app.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.26599999999999,
          "end": 104.533,
          "en": "in that backend folder and keep that process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.533,
          "end": 105.866,
          "en": "up and running as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.866,
          "end": 108.46600000000001,
          "en": "so that you have two running processes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.46600000000001,
          "end": 111.233,
          "en": "because we need both running processes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.233,
          "end": 113.866,
          "en": "in order to connect to the backend here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.96600000000001,
          "end": 117.366,
          "en": "And with that, let's connect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.366,
          "end": 121.4,
          "en": "And let's start by fetching some available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.3,
          "end": 125.8,
          "en": "so that here in this bottom box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.8,
          "end": 129.533,
          "en": "we show a list of places that can be picked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.533,
          "end": 132.333,
          "en": "and selected by the website visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.533,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "Unlike before in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 138.5,
          "en": "where we worked on a similar project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.5,
          "end": 143,
          "en": "those places are now not part of the React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143,
          "end": 145.966,
          "en": "The data and the images for those places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.966,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "are not part of that project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 151.966,
          "en": "Instead, this data is all stored in the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.966,
          "end": 154.966,
          "en": "and it's accessible through that API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.966,
          "end": 159.166,
          "en": "through those exposed endpoints I mentioned there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.7,
          "end": 165.7,
          "en": "So we need to send a HTTP request from inside our React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.1,
          "end": 169.633,
          "en": "to that backend code to fetch that list of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.53300000000002,
          "end": 172.966,
          "en": "Now here in this starting application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.966,
          "end": 175.1,
          "en": "which I prepared for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.1,
          "end": 179.066,
          "en": "there is a separate AvailablePlaces component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.066,
          "end": 184,
          "en": "that's responsible for displaying those pickable places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184,
          "end": 187.566,
          "en": "And it's here where that place data should be fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.566,
          "end": 190.5,
          "en": "from this dummy backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.5,
          "end": 194.166,
          "en": "that backend API I'm providing as part of this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.166,
          "end": 198.466,
          "en": "Now, previously in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.466,
          "end": 201.966,
          "en": "we for example also fetched data from local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.966,
          "end": 203.5,
          "en": "with the getItem method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.466,
          "end": 208.266,
          "en": "And the great thing about local storage is and was",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.266,
          "end": 210.766,
          "en": "that you can access it synchronously,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.766,
          "end": 213.933,
          "en": "that the data you're fetching is there immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.933,
          "end": 215.5,
          "en": "You don't need to wait for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.466,
          "end": 220.1,
          "en": "Therefore, when using local storage we could for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.1,
          "end": 223.4,
          "en": "manage the available places here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.4,
          "end": 227.933,
          "en": "with state by importing useState from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.066,
          "end": 231.333,
          "en": "so that we have our state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.333,
          "end": 235.966,
          "en": "And then here we have the available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.966,
          "end": 238.36599999999999,
          "en": "in this case here, in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.86599999999999,
          "end": 242.266,
          "en": "And this array of available places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.266,
          "end": 247.266,
          "en": "which we have initially could be fetched from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.36599999999999,
          "end": 249.7,
          "en": "So here, if we're fetching those places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.7,
          "end": 251.5,
          "en": "and we get back those places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.5,
          "end": 253.666,
          "en": "and let's assume that is an array of places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.666,
          "end": 256.533,
          "en": "then we could use those places here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.133,
          "end": 260.266,
          "en": "Now that works with local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.266,
          "end": 263.966,
          "en": "but not when getting the data from a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.966,
          "end": 266.2,
          "en": "Because when talking to a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.2,
          "end": 270.033,
          "en": "you are sending an HTTP request that needs to travel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.033,
          "end": 273.56600000000003,
          "en": "through the internet to that backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.56600000000003,
          "end": 276.766,
          "en": "and then that backend server needs to do some work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.766,
          "end": 279.06600000000003,
          "en": "and send back a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.06600000000003,
          "end": 281.766,
          "en": "And that all may take some time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.766,
          "end": 284.56600000000003,
          "en": "It's not an instant process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.56600000000003,
          "end": 288.83299999999997,
          "en": "It may take a couple of milliseconds or even seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.83299999999997,
          "end": 291.9,
          "en": "But the problem is that if this process here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.9,
          "end": 294.466,
          "en": "takes milliseconds or seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.466,
          "end": 298.266,
          "en": "you can't wait for that data here in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.266,
          "end": 300.8,
          "en": "because this component function does not wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.8,
          "end": 302.5,
          "en": "for any data to arrive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.5,
          "end": 304.766,
          "en": "Instead, it executes pretty much instantly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.766,
          "end": 307,
          "en": "in one single step you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.2,
          "end": 312.3,
          "en": "So if this places data is not available initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.3,
          "end": 316.2,
          "en": "you must first render this component without that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.2,
          "end": 320.2,
          "en": "and then update it once that data is available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 321.066,
          "end": 324.233,
          "en": "So therefore, what we need to do here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.233,
          "end": 329.033,
          "en": "we should start with an empty array as our initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.033,
          "end": 332.766,
          "en": "and then we can use those available places down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 334.033,
          "end": 337.233,
          "en": "And then we need to send an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 337.233,
          "end": 340.766,
          "en": "and update this state once the data is there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 341.8,
          "end": 346.06600000000003,
          "en": "so that we re-render the UI and update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}